# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and left to the platform
# in the working tree — except where the bytes themselves are the subject.

* text=auto

# Transcript fixtures are a *format* under test, not source code. Real
# transcripts are LF-delimited JSONL, and `truncated.jsonl` deliberately ends
# mid-record with no trailing newline so the reader's partial-line handling has
# something real to handle. A CRLF checkout would change the byte offsets these
# tests reason about and make them pass or fail for reasons unrelated to the
# code — which has already happened once in this repository, to a README
# assertion.
*.jsonl -text

# Design exports are generated artefacts; leave them exactly as they arrived.
resources/*.dc.html -text
